# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SyMoNeuRaL repository policy
#
# TRACKED   : SyMoNeuRaL work product - documents, curated recipes, bbappends,
#             layer config, scan tools - AND every acquired upstream tree at its
#             pinned commit (acquisition/source-lock.json).
# UNTRACKED : pin stores (.gitpins), ALL build output, caches, secrets, weights.
#
# Rule is deny-by-default: ignore everything heavy, then explicitly re-admit
# the directories that are actually ours.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Acquired upstream source IS committed - it is the product being built, and
# the objective is every tree in this repository at its pin (SOURCES-100).
# Nothing under Symoneural-*/src/*/source/ is ignored. Each tree's own .git is
# MOVED beside it into .gitpins/ (the pin store: local provenance, never pushed)
# so the files are plain content here and the pin has one source of truth.
**/.gitpins/

# ALL build output, then re-admit the devtool workspace (our recipes/appends)
Symoneural-*/build/*

# Fetch + sstate caches
Symoneural-*/downloads/
Symoneural-*/sstate-cache*/

# Staged product output
Symoneural-*/prod/bin/*
Symoneural-*/prod/lib/*

# Generated tree inventories - large and regenerable
*.tree.txt

# Python bytecode from the scanner suite
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Sandbox scaffolding (NOT project files)
# These paths are character devices (/dev/null shims, owner nobody:nogroup)
# injected by the execution environment. Git cannot stage a device node, but
# they otherwise appear as untracked noise. Listed narrowly and never covering
# a path that could be a real project file.
#
# .gitmodules is DELIBERATELY NOT listed. A repository carrying submodule
# configuration must never silently ignore it.
.bashrc
.bash_profile
.profile
.zshrc
.zprofile
.gitconfig
.mcp.json
.ripgreprc
.idea
.vscode
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS - deny by pattern, not by discipline.
#
# No secret has ever been tracked here: /etc/symoneural/*.env is root-owned 0600
# and lives OUTSIDE this repository by design (R13). The full-history scan that
# backs that statement is tools/pre-publish-audit.sh (filenames and content, all
# commits, outside the verified upstream trees) and it is re-run before every
# push; its last recorded PASS is cited in docs/maintenance/. (The "231 paths ever
# added" figure that used to sit here predates SOURCES-100 - the repository now
# tracks ~291,000 files, most of them acquired upstream source at its pin.) These
# rules exist so the statement stays true by construction rather than by memory.
#
# Treat this repository as if it were public even while it is private: a repo
# that is published once is forked, cached and archived, and making it private
# afterwards undoes none of that.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.env
!*.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
# Key files whose name does not end in a dotted extension. `*.key` matches
# "foo.key" but NOT ".audit-key" - hyphen before the word, no dot. Found by
# testing the pattern against a real filename rather than reading it.
*-key
.audit-key
*_key
*.hmac
*.kdbx
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
credentials*
secrets*
*token*.json
*.secret

# Provisioned secret material, if ever mirrored into the tree by mistake
etc/symoneural/
**/symoneural/*.env
**/licensing/*.pub
**/licensing/*.priv

# Model weights never enter git (SYMON_MODELS_DIR = /home/google/symoneural-models)
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.bin.gguf
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
# Weights that hide behind generic extensions (2026-09-15). `*.bin` as a whole is
# too broad to deny (firmware blobs, CUDA probes), so the model-shaped names are
# listed: the register's whisper model is ggml-base.en.bin, and HF checkpoints are
# pytorch_model*.bin / consolidated*.bin. tools/pre-publish-audit.sh checks the same
# shapes and, for anything tracked over 1 MB, the GGUF / safetensors magic bytes.
ggml-*.bin
pytorch_model*.bin
consolidated*.bin
*.h5
*.tflite
*.npz
*.msgpack
*.engine

# Local operator scratch
*.local
.env.*
developer_settings.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERSONAL DATA - never tracked.
#
# Org member exports carry names, email addresses and roles for OTHER PEOPLE.
# That is personal data, and a private repository is not a safe home for it:
# repos get cloned, backed up, mirrored, and sometimes opened up later. The
# knowledge of what the file is lives in ops/README.md; the file itself lives
# outside this tree at /home/google/symoneural-ops (0700).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*members*.csv
*users*.csv
*roster*.csv
*seats*.csv
ops/*.csv
!ops/*-usage-*.csv
# host regression binaries built in place by Symoneural-API/app/tests/native/Makefile
Symoneural-API/app/tests/native/test_gpulock
Symoneural-API/app/tests/native/test_rack
Symoneural-API/app/tests/native/test_unit
Symoneural-API/app/tests/native/test_api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL MODEL STORE AND WORKING TREES (2026-09-17) - deny the DIRECTORY, not the
# extension.
#
# /models/ is not a folder this repository made: it is a mount point. /etc/fstab
# line 6 mounts UUID=baf9f6dc-... (/dev/nvme0n1p7, 143 GB) there, and it holds
# 35 GB of weights (gpt-oss-20b, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-NVFP4). The extension rules above
# do NOT protect it: a Hugging Face snapshot also carries config.json, README.md,
# LICENSE and model.safetensors.index.json, and a Hub cache stores its blobs as
# blobs/<sha256> with no extension at all. One `git add .` would stage third-party
# model cards and, for the cache shape, the weights themselves. Whether the
# partition should be re-mounted outside the repository is an fstab decision for
# Garrett; this line makes the git hazard zero either way.
/models/

# FreeToken/ is a 6.8 GB working clone of FlashML-org/FreeToken at 0.1.3 with a
# .venv - NOT the acquired tree (that is Symoneural-Adaptive-Fabric/src/freetoken/
# source/FreeToken at pin 9db1a39455a3). It is deliberately left in place rather
# than moved: its console scripts carry absolute shebangs into this path, so a
# move breaks a tool the 17 Sep test plan (T0) invokes.
/FreeToken/

# Chat-output archives dropped in the root while moving files between machines.
/files*.zip
